			x: -2.5d
			y: -0.5d
			description: ["The Backrooms is a mod based on the infamous internet Creepypasta \"the Backrooms\". Set in a dingy, mildewy office space that continues forever in similar but different looking patterns. This creepypasta gave rise to the now renouned \"liminal space\" art style. Essentially these are places that are familiar, but feel odd. Psychologically similar is the \"uncanny valley\" effect, which is based on people who look mostly human, but are just creepy enough to instill a sense of dread. This is because evolutionarily humans evolved to recognize faces, predators from friends, and so a human face appearing just slightly different enables our fight-or-flight reaction because it gives us just enough time to recognize something as human, before we come to the conclusion that this is something to be feared. This is similar to how a liminal space operates, instead it's done with places instead of people. Places we most trust are typically low-crime areas we regularly interact with, or have fond memories of. That's why the poolrooms level is so infamous. Many go to places like Great Wolf Lodge to have fun and enjoy a family vacation, however that trust can be abused by slightly tweaking the environment so you feel like something is just a little off, or maybe even very off. The contradiction between your fondness of the place, and the idea of how much fun it would be to just go for a swim, compared to the sense of dread and urgency, is what gives these places their sense of horror. Many anomalies appear, such as odd door placement, and weird signs on the walls the deeper you go. There are levels as well, including the infamous level 37 or \"poolrooms\". Many of which are not present in the mod. This mod adds a few level-specific entities like the Duller, which appears in the Poolrooms, and the Smiler. The \"bosses\" or entities in this modpack are not quite difficult as they where meant to be fought with little armor (essentially you run away from them instead of fighting)."]
			id: "2A76B601AF305DEC"
